{#-
  Full-screen search overlay, from design-source/partials/search.html.

  Site search is not built (features.searchEnabled is false), so no input is
  rendered — only the honest copy and the shortcut links the export's own
  README §8.9 describes. The export ships the input unconditionally, which
  leaves a focusable control that does nothing on all 63 pages; that is the
  same failure the disabled forms avoid (CHECKLIST H). js/ui.js is null-guarded
  so the overlay still takes focus with the input absent.

  DESIGN: structure fixed. CONTENT: shortcuts from _data/chrome.json.
-#}
<div class="search-ov" role="dialog" aria-modal="true" aria-label="Search">
  <div class="so-top">{% image "logos/logo-tight-light.png", "", "8rem", [160, 320], "lazy", "logo-44" %}<button class="drawer-x" type="button" aria-label="Close search" data-search-close>&#10005;</button></div>
  {% if features.searchEnabled %}
  <label for="site-search">Search uncost.org</label>
  <input id="site-search" type="search" placeholder="Try &ldquo;shelter&rdquo; or &ldquo;pledge&rdquo;&hellip;" autocomplete="off">
  {% endif %}
  <div class="so-note">Site search is planned &mdash; it arrives with the dashboard build. Until then, these get you everywhere:</div>
  <p class="so-receipts"><a class="u-btn u-btn--ink" href="/receipts/">Search the Receipts</a></p>
  <div class="so-links">{% for link in chrome.searchShortcuts %}<a href="{{ link.url }}">{{ link.label }}</a>{% endfor %}</div>
</div>
